WEBVTT

1
00:01:47.491 --> 00:01:50.131
<i>No! Oh...!</i>

2
00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.737
Come on!

3
00:02:00.303 --> 00:02:01.873
Come on!

4
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.516
- Open the door! Open the door!
- Let us in!

5
00:03:30.327 --> 00:03:31.704
Get up.

6
00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:39.868
Gimme another day.
One more day.

7
00:03:39.869 --> 00:03:42.171
One more day
isn't going to make any difference.

8
00:03:42.172 --> 00:03:45.119
Oh, please!
Just give me some more meds!

9
00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:49.020
You had your meds, Hal.
You're getting worse.

10
00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:51.216
Put me back in quarantine.

11
00:03:52.082 --> 00:03:55.029
Just until tomorrow. I'll get better.

12
00:03:58.188 --> 00:04:00.168
You're not gonna get better, Hal.

13
00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:06.797
I'll... I'll take the walk.
It's my choice.

14
00:04:08.298 --> 00:04:09.902
Not today.

15
00:04:12.102 --> 00:04:15.572
You can't do this! It's, it's my choice!

16
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.551
It's my job.

17
00:04:19.175 --> 00:04:21.621
- Make your peace.
- Mason!

18
00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:27.592
He tested positive, Sam.

19
00:04:31.421 --> 00:04:32.866
He has a choice!

20
00:04:34.057 --> 00:04:35.297
Let him walk!

21
00:04:35.859 --> 00:04:39.432
He'll just come back. They always do.

22
00:04:39.663 --> 00:04:42.143
We can't let him infect
the rest of the colony.

23
00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:45.310
Mason!

24
00:04:48.571 --> 00:04:49.914
This isn't right.

25
00:04:50.173 --> 00:04:52.119
This is survival!

26
00:05:23.073 --> 00:05:24.780
It's nothing personal.

27
00:05:32.849 --> 00:05:34.988
His time was up. That's all, Sam.

28
00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.140
<i>In this place, we live in fear
of the common cold.</i>

29
00:05:50.166 --> 00:05:53.477
<i>The last flu wiped out twenty people
in less than a week.</i>

30
00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:57.148
<i>So, now we've got rules.</i>

31
00:05:57.941 --> 00:06:00.547
<i>You get sick, you go into quarantine.</i>

32
00:06:01.111 --> 00:06:04.149
<i>If you don't get better,
you've got a choice...</i>

33
00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:10.159
<i>A bullet...
or a long walk in the snow.</i>

34
00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:14.665
<i>At least that's how
it's supposed to work.</i>

35
00:06:19.896 --> 00:06:23.070
<i>After the snow started
the lucky ones found places like this.</i>

36
00:06:25.168 --> 00:06:28.081
<i>Places where life could exist
underneath the ice.</i>

37
00:06:34.411 --> 00:06:37.949
<i>When I got here, we were hundreds
living on top of each other.</i>

38
00:06:39.749 --> 00:06:42.753
<i>Everyone just thankful they'd made
it out of the cities alive.</i>

39
00:06:46.055 --> 00:06:50.026
<i>When the food ran out,
most of the people in the world died.</i>

40
00:06:50.827 --> 00:06:52.932
<i>But not the people in this place.</i>

41
00:06:53.563 --> 00:06:56.134
<i>Where seeds were stored underground...</i>

42
00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:59.340
<i>Kept safe. For a better day.</i>

43
00:07:20.056 --> 00:07:22.593
<i>Some people, they talk about a place...</i>

44
00:07:23.026 --> 00:07:27.634
<i>paradise blue skies
and birds as far as you can see.</i>

45
00:07:29.065 --> 00:07:30.635
<i>Those are just stories.</i>

46
00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.103
<i>Everybody knows that.</i>

47
00:07:38.508 --> 00:07:40.078
<i>So we hold on.</i>

48
00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.589
<i>Hibernating,
like the last dark age.</i>

49
00:07:46.082 --> 00:07:48.653
<i>But it's not the cold
we need to worry about.</i>

50
00:07:50.286 --> 00:07:51.594
<i>It's each other.</i>

51
00:07:52.388 --> 00:07:54.323
- Briggs.
- What's up, Sam?

52
00:07:54.324 --> 00:07:56.930
- I need to talk to you...
- Look. Don't start. Hal knew the rules.

53
00:07:57.126 --> 00:07:59.361
His blood test was positive
and he wasn't getting any better.

54
00:07:59.362 --> 00:08:01.630
We don't have the meds
to keep fighting this flu anymore.

55
00:08:01.631 --> 00:08:03.031
And we can't risk another outbreak.

56
00:08:03.032 --> 00:08:05.567
But why do we leave it to the one guy
who loves to pull the trigger?

57
00:08:05.568 --> 00:08:08.136
Look. This colony started
with over 400 people.

58
00:08:08.137 --> 00:08:09.938
And I have done too much surface time

59
00:08:09.939 --> 00:08:12.407
with a shotgun in one hand
and a shovel in the other.

60
00:08:12.408 --> 00:08:14.820
I've had my fill of blood in the snow.
You understand?

61
00:08:14.944 --> 00:08:16.445
Now, Mason is just doing
what has to be done.

62
00:08:16.446 --> 00:08:18.926
Yeah, but he's not doing it right.
He didn't give him a choice.

63
00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.263
Hal wanted to walk.
Not take a bullet.

64
00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:30.696
Well, right now,
we have a bigger issue.

65
00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.740
Calling Colony 5,
this is Colony 7. Over.

66
00:08:44.374 --> 00:08:47.082
Colony 5, this is Colony 7.
Come on, guys, over...

67
00:08:47.544 --> 00:08:50.045
- What's up?
- SOS loop from Colony 5.

68
00:08:50.046 --> 00:08:51.213
- SOS?
- SOS.

69
00:08:51.214 --> 00:08:53.125
- You sure it's Five?
- It's got to be. It's their code.

70
00:08:53.349 --> 00:08:54.657
Marcus always checks in.

71
00:08:54.784 --> 00:08:56.285
When was the last time
you had contact with him?

72
00:08:56.286 --> 00:08:59.267
About seven days. They said they
were gonna be down for radio repairs.

73
00:08:59.455 --> 00:09:01.992
And they've been dead air
until about an hour ago.

74
00:09:06.629 --> 00:09:09.097
Okay. Make an announcement.

75
00:09:09.098 --> 00:09:11.166
General meeting in the main hall
in thirty minutes.

76
00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:13.001
- Okay, for who?
- For everyone.

77
00:09:13.002 --> 00:09:14.845
I want you to go see Viktor, Sam.

78
00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:17.076
He's having a problem
with the livestock.

79
00:09:20.577 --> 00:09:22.022
Right.

80
00:09:22.946 --> 00:09:27.049
<i>Attention. All colonists report
to the main hall in thirty minutes.</i>

81
00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:31.863
<i>I repeat. All colonists please report
to the main hall in thirty minutes.</i>

82
00:09:31.988 --> 00:09:33.194
<i>Thank you.</i>

83
00:09:47.904 --> 00:09:50.145
You're gonna try
and save these rabbits too?

84
00:09:53.509 --> 00:09:55.386
Another stillborn litter.

85
00:09:56.646 --> 00:09:59.593
They need protein.
Just like us.

86
00:10:01.284 --> 00:10:02.661
How many are left?

87
00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:05.162
Twelve in all.

88
00:10:05.388 --> 00:10:10.394
But this here... is the only female.

89
00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.034
You know you're screwed
when even the rabbits won't fuck.

90
00:10:18.134 --> 00:10:19.841
Let me see what I can get from Kai.

91
00:10:25.742 --> 00:10:27.744
Mason! What's going on?

92
00:10:29.178 --> 00:10:31.738
- What are you talking about?
- What happened out there with Hal?

93
00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.786
Sam come running to you?

94
00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.097
What gives you the right
to take away a man's choice?

95
00:10:48.364 --> 00:10:50.366
His choice was made
when he tested positive.

96
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.735
That is not how we do things.
We give people a choice.

97
00:10:53.736 --> 00:10:56.580
It's theirs to make regardless
of the outcome.

98
00:10:57.006 --> 00:11:00.886
Till they come back.
Till the food runs out.

99
00:11:02.945 --> 00:11:07.553
It's not a problem.
Until it's a problem.

100
00:11:09.085 --> 00:11:11.588
You gave me this job to do.

101
00:11:13.423 --> 00:11:14.993
Now let me do it.

102
00:11:18.828 --> 00:11:20.028
Mason!

103
00:11:20.029 --> 00:11:21.440
You know...

104
00:11:22.699 --> 00:11:24.099
You'd think for someone who served...

105
00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.137
with you you're give them
a little more respect.

106
00:11:58.901 --> 00:12:00.039
Almost had you.

107
00:12:00.503 --> 00:12:01.982
No you didn't.

108
00:12:06.709 --> 00:12:07.983
What do you need?

109
00:12:08.411 --> 00:12:09.981
Soy pellets.

110
00:12:10.346 --> 00:12:12.155
The rabbits aren't doing so hot.

111
00:12:35.605 --> 00:12:36.948
Where's this?

112
00:12:38.374 --> 00:12:41.150
Uh, somewhere in Spain I think.

113
00:12:44.814 --> 00:12:46.418
You never give up, do you?

114
00:12:47.583 --> 00:12:53.033
No. No one thought Briggs could fix that
link to that old satellite, but he did.

115
00:12:55.024 --> 00:12:56.162
So?

116
00:12:57.627 --> 00:13:01.363
So all that weather
modification tech is out there.

117
00:13:01.364 --> 00:13:03.970
It's just buried under the ice.

118
00:13:05.067 --> 00:13:07.308
Well, that's where it should stay.

119
00:13:08.104 --> 00:13:10.071
- Buried.
- Sam.

120
00:13:10.072 --> 00:13:12.407
Somewhere, someone...
is working on a fix.

121
00:13:12.408 --> 00:13:14.752
And when there's a thaw,
I'm gonna find it.

122
00:13:18.347 --> 00:13:19.792
Will you take me with you?

123
00:13:19.949 --> 00:13:23.021
There's not a lot of choice down here.
You'll have to do.

124
00:13:29.992 --> 00:13:31.300
Hal is gone.

125
00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:39.342
Well, we live and die by our rules, Sam.

126
00:13:46.108 --> 00:13:47.519
We should get to the meeting.

127
00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.113
Breathe slowly.
You can't cough. Okay.

128
00:14:19.442 --> 00:14:22.177
Hey, I fixed that crack
in that old vent for you.

129
00:14:22.178 --> 00:14:23.816
Thanks, Sam. That's great.

130
00:14:25.648 --> 00:14:27.025
Dex?

131
00:14:29.852 --> 00:14:33.163
- You all right?
- Yeah. Yeah. I'm, I'm good.

132
00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:37.594
- You're not looking so hot.
- No, no. Up... it's good. Fine.

133
00:14:38.127 --> 00:14:40.107
Maybe you should go back
to your room, huh?

134
00:15:12.728 --> 00:15:14.332
Alright. Listen up.

135
00:15:15.331 --> 00:15:18.676
A few hours ago we received
a distress signal from Colony 5.

136
00:15:21.504 --> 00:15:24.144
They haven't responded
to any radio calls.

137
00:15:25.174 --> 00:15:28.986
Given that Colony 3 shuttered last year,
I think they're worth checking up on.

138
00:15:29.912 --> 00:15:32.791
Cooper, I want you to see what kind
of radio parts we have to spare.

139
00:15:32.982 --> 00:15:35.929
- Okay.
- We've got nothing to spare.

140
00:15:36.986 --> 00:15:39.364
Mason, we're sending a team
and I'm leading it.

141
00:15:39.789 --> 00:15:41.632
I need two volunteers.

142
00:15:43.426 --> 00:15:45.560
What if they've been hit
with a new flu?

143
00:15:45.561 --> 00:15:47.063
We'll take all precautions.

144
00:15:47.163 --> 00:15:49.064
We'll go into quarantine
when we get back.

145
00:15:49.065 --> 00:15:50.498
That's what it's there for.

146
00:15:50.499 --> 00:15:51.978
Quarantine's a fucking joke.

147
00:15:52.535 --> 00:15:54.276
We're barely surviving here.

148
00:15:54.804 --> 00:15:57.105
We need to take care
of our own, Briggs.

149
00:15:57.106 --> 00:16:01.042
We made a pact with Colony 5
and we need to look after each other.

150
00:16:01.043 --> 00:16:03.353
Yes, we did. And we're going.

151
00:16:03.612 --> 00:16:04.989
End of discussion.

152
00:16:09.151 --> 00:16:10.687
Dexter.

153
00:16:12.188 --> 00:16:14.862
I need a skilled set of hands
with me out there.

154
00:16:19.362 --> 00:16:20.636
I'll go.

155
00:16:25.134 --> 00:16:27.978
Dex needs to stay
in case the turbines break down.

156
00:16:29.972 --> 00:16:31.280
Thank you, Sam.

157
00:16:33.509 --> 00:16:34.988
Anyone else?

158
00:16:35.211 --> 00:16:36.747
Look at me...

159
00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:39.623
Anyone?

160
00:16:40.182 --> 00:16:43.459
- Take me.
- Graydon, no...

161
00:16:44.653 --> 00:16:46.021
- Please don't go...
- No, I know...

162
00:16:46.022 --> 00:16:48.502
I haven't logged a lot of surface time,
but I can do it.

163
00:16:50.493 --> 00:16:53.235
Thank you, Graydon. You'll do well.

164
00:16:56.065 --> 00:16:57.373
Alright.

165
00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:00.174
Kai will be in charge until I'm back.

166
00:17:00.803 --> 00:17:02.137
Rations are still in effect,

167
00:17:02.138 --> 00:17:05.176
although I've authorized regular
portions for the children.

168
00:17:05.341 --> 00:17:09.221
Work details continue as usual.
We'll be in touch by radio.

169
00:17:12.014 --> 00:17:13.357
She's sick...

170
00:17:14.583 --> 00:17:15.857
Come on...

171
00:17:16.385 --> 00:17:17.693
Get her out of here!

172
00:17:42.111 --> 00:17:44.145
Quarantine until further notice.

173
00:17:44.146 --> 00:17:46.126
It's okay, sweetie, don't worry.

174
00:17:46.549 --> 00:17:47.926
It's okay...

175
00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.360
You really should have said
something earlier, Dex.

176
00:17:59.929 --> 00:18:01.738
- They're done, Briggs.
- They're sick.

177
00:18:01.864 --> 00:18:03.434
And we follow procedure.

178
00:18:03.866 --> 00:18:05.733
They just put the whole colony at risk.

179
00:18:05.734 --> 00:18:07.268
We need to give them
a test right now.

180
00:18:07.269 --> 00:18:10.405
We're gonna wait until I get back
and see if they've done any better.

181
00:18:10.406 --> 00:18:12.140
Until then Kai's in charge.

182
00:18:12.141 --> 00:18:14.485
You really think
she can make the tough calls?

183
00:18:14.944 --> 00:18:17.447
That's really not
your decision to make, is it?

184
00:18:19.548 --> 00:18:20.959
Are we clear?

185
00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:22.990
Crystal.

186
00:19:01.123 --> 00:19:03.000
Mom!

187
00:19:34.823 --> 00:19:36.166
Oh my...

188
00:20:03.852 --> 00:20:05.263
You okay?

189
00:20:06.055 --> 00:20:07.659
Yeah.

190
00:20:09.058 --> 00:20:10.799
That fucking dream.

191
00:20:13.229 --> 00:20:15.038
It wasn't your fault.

192
00:20:45.694 --> 00:20:47.469
Would you come back to bed?

193
00:21:27.736 --> 00:21:29.909
<i>The world froze over a long time ago.</i>

194
00:21:30.973 --> 00:21:33.954
<i>So long ago that I can't remember
the warmth of the sun.</i>

195
00:21:37.313 --> 00:21:39.350
<i>I heard the stories growing up...</i>

196
00:21:40.382 --> 00:21:43.363
<i>How the planet grew hotter
as our fuel was burned.</i>

197
00:21:44.486 --> 00:21:47.023
<i>How we made towers
to work the weather.</i>

198
00:21:49.258 --> 00:21:52.899
<i>But the truth is... one day...</i>

199
00:21:53.295 --> 00:21:55.104
<i>it started to snow.</i>

200
00:21:56.432 --> 00:21:57.843
<i>And it never stopped.</i>

201
00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:29.541
Is that what I think it is?

202
00:22:30.866 --> 00:22:32.675
Weather modification.

203
00:22:34.536 --> 00:22:36.641
Never seen one this close.

204
00:22:39.808 --> 00:22:41.310
You think it still works?

205
00:22:43.212 --> 00:22:46.056
It did its damage a long time ago.

206
00:23:35.664 --> 00:23:37.007
We got to cross this thing?

207
00:23:38.867 --> 00:23:40.471
Unless you wanna go down there...

208
00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.812
We make our way around to the left!

209
00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:25.918
Yeah.

210
00:24:48.203 --> 00:24:49.739
Watch your step.

211
00:25:15.564 --> 00:25:16.941
Guys!

212
00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.343
What is that?

213
00:26:07.449 --> 00:26:09.190
What the hell's he doing out here?

214
00:26:30.505 --> 00:26:32.178
We got to keep moving.

215
00:27:47.382 --> 00:27:49.663
God, how cool would it be to fly one
of these things, huh?

216
00:27:51.186 --> 00:27:52.824
Hey, Briggs, what was this used for?

217
00:27:53.088 --> 00:27:54.722
Med-evac.

218
00:27:54.723 --> 00:27:56.669
It used to airlift people to safety.

219
00:27:59.561 --> 00:28:01.404
Ah, I wish I could've seen that.

220
00:28:03.432 --> 00:28:05.844
Briggs to Colony 7,
Cooper, come in.

221
00:28:08.103 --> 00:28:11.107
<i>Colony 7 here.
Good to hear your voice, Briggs.</i>

222
00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:13.717
Copy that.
Good to hear yours.

223
00:28:14.009 --> 00:28:15.843
We're camped out at the helicopter
for the night,

224
00:28:15.844 --> 00:28:18.256
so we should reach Colony 5
by noon tomorrow.

225
00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:20.059
What about you? Got any news?

226
00:28:20.449 --> 00:28:22.827
<i>Dex and Elena are still in quarantine.</i>

227
00:28:23.018 --> 00:28:25.020
<i>And they're both getting worse.</i>

228
00:28:26.121 --> 00:28:27.688
<i>They have all the symptoms.</i>

229
00:28:27.689 --> 00:28:29.498
<i>Mason's pushing for the test.</i>

230
00:28:30.058 --> 00:28:32.436
Mason knows that's against protocol.

231
00:28:33.061 --> 00:28:35.439
That's why I left Kai in charge.

232
00:28:36.698 --> 00:28:38.974
<i>Yeah, he's not too happy about that.</i>

233
00:28:39.868 --> 00:28:40.972
I know.

234
00:28:41.103 --> 00:28:43.242
There's gonna be some changes
made when I get back.

235
00:28:44.106 --> 00:28:46.609
Cooper, you have my authority
to use force if necessary.

236
00:28:46.775 --> 00:28:49.984
Mason is not to take them
for a walk without my consent.

237
00:28:50.245 --> 00:28:53.920
<i>I understand.
You guys be safe out there, okay?</i>

238
00:28:54.149 --> 00:28:55.389
<i>Over and out.</i>

239
00:28:55.617 --> 00:28:57.119
Over and out.

240
00:29:29.484 --> 00:29:32.055
Should we give you some time alone
with that, or...?

241
00:29:37.692 --> 00:29:38.864
Maybe I do.

242
00:29:45.901 --> 00:29:49.041
You know, Sam, we're not too
far from where I found you.

243
00:29:51.273 --> 00:29:52.775
Yeah.

244
00:29:53.108 --> 00:29:54.610
What were you doin' out here?

245
00:29:57.179 --> 00:29:58.852
Well... it was a long time ago.

246
00:29:59.581 --> 00:30:01.060
Go on, tell him.

247
00:30:02.150 --> 00:30:03.390
We got all night.

248
00:30:07.255 --> 00:30:10.702
Um... my family, um...

249
00:30:11.660 --> 00:30:14.300
we were holed up about
forty miles north of here.

250
00:30:15.130 --> 00:30:16.964
In a mine.

251
00:30:16.965 --> 00:30:18.672
Uh, just us and...

252
00:30:19.401 --> 00:30:23.178
some mining families,
a couple old-timers.

253
00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:29.111
We, uh, got supplies in there...
shoveled the entrance out every day.

254
00:30:32.547 --> 00:30:36.825
Eventually, the supplies ran out.
Food ran out.

255
00:30:41.122 --> 00:30:44.433
So after we ate the horses
and the dogs...

256
00:30:46.962 --> 00:30:50.705
my dad and the other men went
into the city to go get some help, but...

257
00:30:52.067 --> 00:30:54.638
They never came back, so...

258
00:30:57.906 --> 00:30:59.749
And people started dying, and...

259
00:31:01.109 --> 00:31:03.885
The way things were going,
I needed to get them out of there.

260
00:31:04.012 --> 00:31:05.719
My mother and my sister...

261
00:31:08.016 --> 00:31:10.121
I figured we had a better
chance out there.

262
00:31:13.188 --> 00:31:16.192
Anyway, uh, the storm came up and...

263
00:31:17.592 --> 00:31:20.539
we got separated,
and I never saw them again.

264
00:31:22.330 --> 00:31:25.470
I'd be dead too
if Briggs hadn't found me.

265
00:31:26.167 --> 00:31:30.138
You were a boy, Sam.
You did the best you could.

266
00:31:32.774 --> 00:31:34.014
Yeah.

267
00:32:34.903 --> 00:32:36.541
Hey, what is this?

268
00:32:37.806 --> 00:32:39.926
You guys that's blood!
We shouldn't be going in there!

269
00:32:40.175 --> 00:32:42.135
You came here to help.
That's what we're gonna do.

270
00:32:52.887 --> 00:32:54.025
You smell that?

271
00:32:55.223 --> 00:32:56.463
Smoke.

272
00:33:41.403 --> 00:33:44.714
You know, maybe one
of us should just stay top-side, huh?

273
00:33:45.140 --> 00:33:46.744
We stick together.

274
00:33:47.442 --> 00:33:48.944
You're coming.

275
00:33:51.446 --> 00:33:52.925
Right.

276
00:34:39.160 --> 00:34:42.107
- How many were there last count?
- Fifty.

277
00:34:42.697 --> 00:34:45.109
Not so much of a welcoming
committee this time.

278
00:35:12.060 --> 00:35:13.664
What the fuck happened here?

279
00:35:19.367 --> 00:35:22.905
Hey. You remember how to use this?

280
00:35:24.105 --> 00:35:26.085
- Yeah.
- You sure?

281
00:35:30.011 --> 00:35:32.514
- Let's move, okay?
- This way.

282
00:36:21.062 --> 00:36:22.473
They're all dead.

283
00:36:23.064 --> 00:36:24.509
We don't know that for sure.

284
00:36:29.938 --> 00:36:31.542
What the fuck was that?

285
00:37:03.571 --> 00:37:05.107
Someone's alive.

286
00:37:10.445 --> 00:37:12.885
- It's coming from over here...
- Sam. Wait, wait, wait, wait.

287
00:37:25.093 --> 00:37:26.265
In here.

288
00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:35.168
This door has taken a lot
of punishment.

289
00:37:35.169 --> 00:37:38.582
Shit. Hey, c'mon,
let's get outta here, huh?

290
00:37:38.706 --> 00:37:41.585
Hey, find a spine, boy.

291
00:38:10.405 --> 00:38:11.748
You got it?

292
00:38:44.505 --> 00:38:45.813
What, is he dead?

293
00:39:01.122 --> 00:39:02.897
Oh shit!

294
00:39:03.591 --> 00:39:06.299
Calm down! Calm down! Calm down!

295
00:39:09.530 --> 00:39:12.132
- Don't! Don't!
- Easy. Easy.

296
00:39:12.133 --> 00:39:15.046
- Please, don't...
- We're here to help.

297
00:39:16.070 --> 00:39:18.880
Please. Don't, don't, don't.

298
00:39:19.607 --> 00:39:22.349
It's okay. Calm down.

299
00:39:24.312 --> 00:39:25.985
Are you hurt?

300
00:39:27.048 --> 00:39:29.722
- Are they gone?
- Who?

301
00:39:30.585 --> 00:39:32.690
The door! Lock the door.

302
00:39:33.821 --> 00:39:35.095
Get the door!

303
00:39:38.126 --> 00:39:39.537
He needs water.

304
00:39:44.565 --> 00:39:46.977
No, easy. Go easy, easy, easy, easy.

305
00:39:49.704 --> 00:39:50.978
What's your name?

306
00:39:51.506 --> 00:39:54.077
- Leland.
- Leland.

307
00:39:54.242 --> 00:39:56.410
Have you got any food? I'm so hungry.

308
00:39:56.411 --> 00:39:58.721
Yeah. I've got something here.

309
00:39:58.846 --> 00:40:00.450
How long have you been locked in here?

310
00:40:00.581 --> 00:40:02.185
I, I don't know.

311
00:40:03.050 --> 00:40:04.154
Days.

312
00:40:04.552 --> 00:40:07.795
Is there anyone else?
Is anyone else alive?

313
00:40:09.023 --> 00:40:10.559
Define alive.

314
00:40:14.228 --> 00:40:15.798
It's good.

315
00:40:18.299 --> 00:40:22.042
We're from Colony 7.
We got your distress signal.

316
00:40:22.570 --> 00:40:24.072
We came to help.

317
00:40:27.408 --> 00:40:28.944
Leland.

318
00:40:30.011 --> 00:40:31.115
What happened?

319
00:40:31.245 --> 00:40:35.819
We fixed the...
steel grid to a new antenna.

320
00:40:36.551 --> 00:40:42.297
When, when it finally worked...
its reach was, was amazing.

321
00:40:44.425 --> 00:40:48.737
We, we received a...
a partial transmission.

322
00:40:57.605 --> 00:40:59.372
You're gonna love this.

323
00:40:59.373 --> 00:41:01.808
I repeat. We have modified
a weather tower

324
00:41:01.809 --> 00:41:04.377
and successfully reversed
the cooling process.

325
00:41:04.378 --> 00:41:07.985
Clouds have receded
to a three mile radius and are expanding.

326
00:41:08.649 --> 00:41:10.219
We have thawed permafrost.

327
00:41:11.185 --> 00:41:15.422
We have melted pack ice.
We now have soil.

328
00:41:15.423 --> 00:41:19.997
We have sun.
We now have the conditions to grow.

329
00:41:20.495 --> 00:41:21.761
But we have no seeds.

330
00:41:21.762 --> 00:41:23.537
If anyone out there can hear this...

331
00:41:23.831 --> 00:41:25.970
I repeat our location. Our location...

332
00:41:26.100 --> 00:41:28.341
Latitude forty seven degrees north...

333
00:41:32.173 --> 00:41:34.210
Is that it? Is that all there is?

334
00:41:37.144 --> 00:41:40.046
We triangulated the, the transmission.

335
00:41:40.047 --> 00:41:42.027
Sent a team to find the source.

336
00:41:43.150 --> 00:41:46.393
But... they never found it.

337
00:41:48.322 --> 00:41:49.995
But somebody found them.

338
00:41:53.094 --> 00:41:56.007
- And followed them right back here...
- Who?

339
00:41:56.497 --> 00:41:58.033
Leland! Who followed you...?

340
00:42:00.001 --> 00:42:03.175
Look at me. Over here.
Show me. On this map.

341
00:42:04.071 --> 00:42:05.551
Where did that
transmission come from?

342
00:42:07.174 --> 00:42:09.176
Point... we're right here.

343
00:42:09.310 --> 00:42:11.881
North... on this line.

344
00:42:12.113 --> 00:42:14.923
And twenty five degrees is here.

345
00:42:15.883 --> 00:42:18.830
South... there.

346
00:42:21.789 --> 00:42:22.961
Listen to me.

347
00:42:24.058 --> 00:42:26.092
We're gonna take you back
to Colony 7 with us.

348
00:42:26.093 --> 00:42:28.562
No! Please, sir.
I, I'm gonna stay here.

349
00:42:28.563 --> 00:42:30.008
Right here... behind this door.

350
00:42:30.932 --> 00:42:32.365
What if they're still here?

351
00:42:32.366 --> 00:42:33.674
There's no one here.

352
00:42:34.936 --> 00:42:37.280
We only knew that you were here
because of the knocking.

353
00:42:40.641 --> 00:42:42.279
Yeah, but I didn't knock.

354
00:42:43.611 --> 00:42:45.113
They're still here!

355
00:42:47.548 --> 00:42:48.882
They're still here.

356
00:42:48.883 --> 00:42:51.851
Radio Colony 7.
You tell them we're on our way back.

357
00:42:51.852 --> 00:42:53.354
- It's time for us to pack up and go.
- Yeah.

358
00:42:53.454 --> 00:42:55.161
- Take anything we can carry.
- Okay...

359
00:42:55.423 --> 00:42:57.164
it's okay. It's alright.

360
00:43:02.630 --> 00:43:04.132
Calling Colony 7.

361
00:43:05.066 --> 00:43:07.137
Colony 7,
can you read me? Over.

362
00:43:09.670 --> 00:43:11.274
Colony 7, come in.

363
00:43:12.707 --> 00:43:15.187
This is Graydon calling in.
Can you read me? Over.

364
00:43:17.044 --> 00:43:18.645
It's not working.

365
00:43:18.646 --> 00:43:20.592
Alright.
We're too deep underground.

366
00:43:20.748 --> 00:43:23.058
We'll radio ahead
to when we get back topside.

367
00:43:24.852 --> 00:43:26.058
You. Leland.

368
00:43:26.487 --> 00:43:27.721
You're coming with us.

369
00:43:27.722 --> 00:43:31.091
You don't understand!
It's safe behind this door!

370
00:43:31.092 --> 00:43:33.094
There's fifty colonists.
You're the only one behind it.

371
00:43:33.227 --> 00:43:37.073
I, I, I couldn't open it.
I, I, I just couldn't.

372
00:43:55.016 --> 00:43:56.552
Get him on his feet.

373
00:43:59.987 --> 00:44:01.489
- No. Please.
- C'mon. Let's go.

374
00:44:08.696 --> 00:44:10.073
What the fuck was that?

375
00:44:20.041 --> 00:44:21.179
Shit...

376
00:44:23.811 --> 00:44:26.155
He locked himself back inside.

377
00:44:26.681 --> 00:44:28.183
C'mon.

378
00:44:34.455 --> 00:44:36.264
Graydon, let's go!

379
00:45:52.133 --> 00:45:56.775
We shouldn't be here.
This has nothing to do with us.

380
00:45:56.904 --> 00:45:58.315
Turn that light out.

381
00:46:37.111 --> 00:46:38.385
Oh my God...

382
00:47:19.587 --> 00:47:20.759
We got to go, Sam.

383
00:47:24.191 --> 00:47:25.363
Now!

384
00:47:41.375 --> 00:47:43.548
Go! Go! Go! Go!

385
00:47:56.790 --> 00:47:58.064
C'mon!

386
00:48:07.534 --> 00:48:09.104
Fuck.

387
00:48:23.050 --> 00:48:24.461
Fuck!

388
00:48:45.873 --> 00:48:47.607
Come on, Sam...

389
00:48:47.608 --> 00:48:48.609
Come on...

390
00:48:50.978 --> 00:48:53.151
Damn... Graydon.

391
00:49:02.323 --> 00:49:04.701
He's gone. We got to move.

392
00:49:04.825 --> 00:49:06.668
Go on. Go!

393
00:49:24.144 --> 00:49:25.555
Go! Go!

394
00:49:33.253 --> 00:49:34.596
Come on!

395
00:49:43.263 --> 00:49:46.073
- Oh! Fuck! I'm out!
- Come on! Go! Go!

396
00:51:31.071 --> 00:51:32.641
Briggs!

397
00:51:35.008 --> 00:51:37.318
Here! Gimme your hand.
Gimme your hand!

398
00:51:45.085 --> 00:51:46.792
There's still people alive down there.

399
00:51:47.221 --> 00:51:48.495
We can't help them, Sam.

400
00:51:49.656 --> 00:51:50.999
We can't help them.

401
00:53:12.873 --> 00:53:13.943
Briggs!

402
00:53:14.141 --> 00:53:15.775
Don't you think
we should keep moving?

403
00:53:15.776 --> 00:53:18.518
No! The temperatures dropping too fast.
We won't make it!

404
00:53:23.217 --> 00:53:24.594
Come on...

405
00:53:40.067 --> 00:53:42.445
- Briggs?
- Yeah?

406
00:53:44.972 --> 00:53:46.383
Those people...

407
00:53:49.109 --> 00:53:50.611
How could they...?

408
00:53:52.546 --> 00:53:54.025
I don't know, Sam.

409
00:53:56.216 --> 00:53:58.253
When people are desperate they'll do...

410
00:53:59.419 --> 00:54:01.592
horrible things to survive.

411
00:54:04.891 --> 00:54:07.098
I told you I was an Army captain...

412
00:54:07.361 --> 00:54:09.466
during the relief effort, right?

413
00:54:10.297 --> 00:54:11.901
Yeah.

414
00:54:13.100 --> 00:54:15.307
Yeah, well,
I never told you what I saw...

415
00:54:16.870 --> 00:54:21.080
when... when people lose
control like that...

416
00:54:22.609 --> 00:54:24.520
When we go feral...

417
00:54:27.147 --> 00:54:29.593
there's nothing human left in us at all.

418
00:54:30.484 --> 00:54:33.158
We might as well
just be a pack of wild dogs.

419
00:54:38.592 --> 00:54:41.060
See, during the relief effort,
we had uh...

420
00:54:41.061 --> 00:54:44.531
twenty thousand people
corralled in a stadium.

421
00:54:47.067 --> 00:54:48.546
Food got handed out.

422
00:54:49.169 --> 00:54:51.046
And the sick got treated.

423
00:54:52.739 --> 00:54:54.776
But when the food ran out..

424
00:54:56.209 --> 00:55:00.157
The people with guns stand taking things
from the people without guns.

425
00:55:01.748 --> 00:55:05.195
And then...
when there was nothing left to take...

426
00:55:07.054 --> 00:55:10.627
they took people upstairs and decided
who would live and who would die.

427
00:55:17.097 --> 00:55:19.737
It was... it's the hunger.

428
00:55:20.701 --> 00:55:23.113
People couldn't take it.
It just drove them mad.

429
00:55:26.106 --> 00:55:28.552
We tried to stop it.
We really did but...

430
00:55:30.210 --> 00:55:31.780
we couldn't.

431
00:55:37.050 --> 00:55:40.497
Me and Mason he was
my squad back then. We, we left.

432
00:55:41.121 --> 00:55:43.101
Tried to find a place
where we could make sure...

433
00:55:43.223 --> 00:55:45.066
nothing like that would happen.

434
00:55:50.564 --> 00:55:52.043
You did.

435
00:55:54.167 --> 00:55:55.737
Maybe.

436
00:55:57.170 --> 00:55:58.843
You did.

437
00:56:05.045 --> 00:56:07.025
That transmission...

438
00:56:09.549 --> 00:56:11.016
When we get back...

439
00:56:11.017 --> 00:56:13.998
we'll patch in to the satellite.
Take a look.

440
00:56:16.423 --> 00:56:18.699
If they've got the sun,
we've got the seeds.

441
00:56:45.352 --> 00:56:46.660
No...

442
00:56:47.020 --> 00:56:49.557
- No, no, no!
- How many?

443
00:56:50.857 --> 00:56:52.165
Twenty!

444
00:56:52.325 --> 00:56:54.134
Maybe more! It's hard to tell!

445
00:56:55.061 --> 00:56:56.472
Oh, fuck.

446
00:57:00.100 --> 00:57:01.333
Our footprints!

447
00:57:01.334 --> 00:57:02.677
Oh shit!
We're gonna lead them right back...

448
00:57:02.903 --> 00:57:05.263
- to the colony...
- We'll stop them at the bridge. Come on.

449
00:57:33.066 --> 00:57:34.374
Come on!

450
00:57:55.489 --> 00:57:56.900
Come on!

451
00:58:12.739 --> 00:58:14.912
- Briggs, what are you doing?
- Stopping 'em!

452
00:58:30.123 --> 00:58:31.466
Block the wind!

453
00:58:53.880 --> 00:58:55.047
- No!
- What?

454
00:58:55.048 --> 00:58:57.551
- The fuse is out!
- Fuck!

455
00:59:00.420 --> 00:59:02.696
- I'm gonna go and relight it.
- The fuck you're doing? Briggs?

456
00:59:02.822 --> 00:59:04.495
Listen to me.
Listen to me. We're fine.

457
00:59:04.624 --> 00:59:06.900
I light it. I come back.
We go home.

458
00:59:07.027 --> 00:59:08.438
It's too late!

459
00:59:17.103 --> 00:59:18.241
Briggs!

460
00:59:30.050 --> 00:59:31.051
Come on.

461
00:59:36.122 --> 00:59:37.863
Come on! Get it done!

462
00:59:38.425 --> 00:59:40.132
Come on! Come on!

463
00:59:52.973 --> 00:59:54.384
Yes.

464
00:59:57.811 --> 01:00:01.315
Come on, you dogs!

465
01:02:29.262 --> 01:02:32.835
Please!
Just give her the goddamn test!

466
01:02:33.533 --> 01:02:35.103
No more tests.

467
01:02:35.401 --> 01:02:39.042
No! Oh no! No.

468
01:02:47.480 --> 01:02:48.959
Mason!

469
01:02:51.885 --> 01:02:53.387
What...

470
01:02:56.990 --> 01:02:59.027
Things are gonna change around here.

471
01:02:59.659 --> 01:03:01.527
Are you fucking crazy?

472
01:03:01.528 --> 01:03:02.529
No.

473
01:03:03.029 --> 01:03:05.134
I'm seeing things clearly.

474
01:03:05.632 --> 01:03:09.401
You know the test is bullshit.
The delay just puts us all at risk.

475
01:03:09.402 --> 01:03:11.382
Drop your gun!

476
01:03:22.615 --> 01:03:24.458
Help!

477
01:03:26.219 --> 01:03:28.199
Help!

478
01:03:29.122 --> 01:03:30.189
Sam?

479
01:03:30.190 --> 01:03:31.498
Sam!

480
01:03:34.327 --> 01:03:35.863
Oh fuck...

481
01:03:39.132 --> 01:03:40.304
Fuck!

482
01:03:54.047 --> 01:03:55.117
Sam!

483
01:03:56.583 --> 01:03:58.859
Sam? Sam?

484
01:03:59.085 --> 01:04:02.191
Come on, come on.

485
01:04:20.807 --> 01:04:22.150
Hey...

486
01:04:22.308 --> 01:04:24.117
You're okay. You're safe.

487
01:04:29.015 --> 01:04:30.653
How long have I been out?

488
01:04:31.017 --> 01:04:32.621
A few hours.

489
01:04:44.230 --> 01:04:47.507
Sam? Where is he?

490
01:04:48.334 --> 01:04:49.836
Where's my boy?

491
01:04:57.577 --> 01:04:58.885
I tried.

492
01:05:02.215 --> 01:05:03.956
No...

493
01:05:05.952 --> 01:05:07.431
No...

494
01:05:08.221 --> 01:05:10.030
We lost Briggs too.

495
01:05:20.166 --> 01:05:21.839
Mason, what are you doing?

496
01:05:25.138 --> 01:05:26.742
There's been a change in command.

497
01:05:27.106 --> 01:05:29.108
We need to take precautions.

498
01:05:29.509 --> 01:05:33.821
Briggs' rules don't work anymore.
We need to be tougher to survive.

499
01:05:34.414 --> 01:05:36.416
From now, rations will be cut in half.

500
01:05:36.549 --> 01:05:40.156
Anyone showing signs of sickness
will be tested immediately.

501
01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:42.499
If you don't pull your weight,

502
01:05:42.889 --> 01:05:44.368
- you don't eat.
- Mason.

503
01:05:46.092 --> 01:05:47.298
Where's Kai?

504
01:05:48.828 --> 01:05:50.034
What happened, Sam?

505
01:05:50.530 --> 01:05:52.009
What happened out there?

506
01:05:56.369 --> 01:05:57.677
They killed them.

507
01:06:00.540 --> 01:06:02.918
Everybody at Colony 5 is dead.

508
01:06:06.012 --> 01:06:08.014
Briggs' come off the bridge.

509
01:06:08.948 --> 01:06:11.155
- Stopped them.
- Stopped who?

510
01:06:11.384 --> 01:06:12.988
These people...

511
01:06:14.187 --> 01:06:17.191
They slaughtered everybody.

512
01:06:18.191 --> 01:06:19.864
For food.

513
01:06:20.193 --> 01:06:21.729
Do you understand?

514
01:06:23.162 --> 01:06:24.529
And they're coming here.

515
01:06:24.530 --> 01:06:26.407
And unless we get out of here...

516
01:06:26.532 --> 01:06:28.034
they will kill us.

517
01:06:29.135 --> 01:06:31.081
And where are we gonna go?

518
01:06:31.704 --> 01:06:33.138
There's a thaw.

519
01:06:33.139 --> 01:06:35.415
I know where it is. Okay.
I can get us out of here.

520
01:06:35.708 --> 01:06:37.016
- I can show you where it is...
- He's in shock.

521
01:06:37.143 --> 01:06:38.977
- I can lead you to where it is.
- Give him a sedative.

522
01:06:38.978 --> 01:06:40.423
Let me show you where it is!

523
01:06:40.747 --> 01:06:42.414
No one is going anywhere.

524
01:06:42.415 --> 01:06:44.216
Viktor, let's go topside.

525
01:06:44.217 --> 01:06:46.561
- You need to listen to me!
- Viktor!

526
01:06:47.020 --> 01:06:48.294
Are you with me?

527
01:06:50.089 --> 01:06:51.466
Mason.

528
01:06:51.691 --> 01:06:53.102
You need to listen to me.

529
01:06:53.860 --> 01:06:55.203
Mason!

530
01:06:57.063 --> 01:06:58.133
Mason!

531
01:07:11.244 --> 01:07:13.087
Sam.

532
01:07:20.286 --> 01:07:21.993
What?

533
01:07:26.292 --> 01:07:27.692
No.

534
01:07:27.693 --> 01:07:29.138
Nothing.

535
01:07:33.099 --> 01:07:36.201
You know, Sam says a lot of things
but he's not a liar.

536
01:07:36.202 --> 01:07:40.048
If he says something's coming for us,
we better be ready for 'em.

537
01:07:43.342 --> 01:07:45.151
Keep an eye on the monitors.

538
01:08:00.293 --> 01:08:02.466
- Sam!
- Kai, are you okay?

539
01:08:02.929 --> 01:08:04.629
- Oh my God! Did he hit you?
- It's fine.

540
01:08:04.630 --> 01:08:06.541
- Did he hit you?
- I'm fine!

541
01:08:09.168 --> 01:08:10.772
Are you okay?

542
01:08:20.680 --> 01:08:22.023
Here. Come here.

543
01:08:25.852 --> 01:08:27.297
What happened out there?

544
01:08:30.623 --> 01:08:32.227
I got to show you something.

545
01:08:47.140 --> 01:08:48.380
Bring up two.

546
01:08:54.780 --> 01:08:56.123
Nothing.

547
01:08:56.249 --> 01:08:58.024
This is bullshit.

548
01:08:59.619 --> 01:09:00.859
Mason!

549
01:09:02.588 --> 01:09:03.896
Sam got away.

550
01:09:05.191 --> 01:09:06.499
And how did he do that?

551
01:09:13.091 --> 01:09:14.399
Rowan..

552
01:09:14.467 --> 01:09:15.969
That little bastard.

553
01:09:16.369 --> 01:09:17.973
Come on! Let's go!

554
01:09:24.143 --> 01:09:25.588
Forty-seven, fifty-five...

555
01:09:25.711 --> 01:09:27.952
- What are you looking for?
- A thaw.

556
01:09:28.381 --> 01:09:30.657
- Come on.
- Sam.

557
01:09:31.784 --> 01:09:34.486
Sam, there's nothing there.
I have already looked.

558
01:09:34.487 --> 01:09:36.057
No, it's here. I know it's here.

559
01:09:36.622 --> 01:09:38.158
Sam.

560
01:09:44.130 --> 01:09:45.108
Come on.

561
01:09:50.469 --> 01:09:51.641
There it is.

562
01:09:52.939 --> 01:09:54.145
Holy shit.

563
01:09:54.440 --> 01:09:55.748
Look.

564
01:09:56.175 --> 01:09:57.518
Oh my God...

565
01:09:58.711 --> 01:10:01.012
That's got to be like eight miles
of blue sky.

566
01:10:01.013 --> 01:10:03.357
Come. Let's go.
Come on. Come on.

567
01:10:03.683 --> 01:10:06.755
They took the weapons,
the maps, everything.

568
01:10:07.720 --> 01:10:09.791
Shit. They didn't take these.

569
01:10:11.324 --> 01:10:12.667
What are you doing, Sam?

570
01:10:14.126 --> 01:10:15.961
Sam, what are you doing?

571
01:10:15.962 --> 01:10:17.062
We need to tell the others...

572
01:10:17.063 --> 01:10:19.509
and we need to get the hell
out of here. Let's go. Come on.

573
01:10:25.137 --> 01:10:28.346
C'mon! C'mon! C'mon! C'mon!

574
01:10:31.177 --> 01:10:33.748
- Going somewhere?
- Yeah.

575
01:10:34.213 --> 01:10:36.253
We're gonna get everyone together
and we're leaving.

576
01:10:37.049 --> 01:10:38.216
No one's leaving.

577
01:10:38.217 --> 01:10:40.254
- Go fuck yourself, Mason.
- Hey, hey...

578
01:10:41.287 --> 01:10:43.521
if we don't leave... right now...

579
01:10:43.522 --> 01:10:46.059
Briggs is gone.
I'm running things now.

580
01:10:47.727 --> 01:10:50.161
When everyone's dead, huh?

581
01:10:50.162 --> 01:10:52.082
And you're King of the fucking castle,
then what?

582
01:10:54.333 --> 01:10:56.040
I'll still be running things.

583
01:11:05.544 --> 01:11:09.014
Oh shit. We're too late.

584
01:11:29.769 --> 01:11:31.874
Oh my God... Oh my,
oh my God, it's Dex.

585
01:11:42.281 --> 01:11:43.760
You believe me now?

586
01:11:44.483 --> 01:11:47.020
Anyone who can fire a weapon,
get 'em to the entrance.

587
01:11:47.153 --> 01:11:50.021
We'll hold them there.
And get everybody else to the vault!

588
01:11:50.022 --> 01:11:51.558
Let's go. Come on!

589
01:12:02.368 --> 01:12:03.735
Come on, buddy. Let's go.

590
01:12:03.736 --> 01:12:05.147
It's gonna be alright.

591
01:12:05.304 --> 01:12:06.942
Come on, guys!

592
01:12:07.807 --> 01:12:09.343
Let's go, let's go!

593
01:12:50.015 --> 01:12:51.926
You lead them straight to us.

594
01:12:56.589 --> 01:12:58.159
They're breaking the hinges.

595
01:13:00.726 --> 01:13:01.830
Fuck...

596
01:13:36.462 --> 01:13:37.839
Behind us!

597
01:14:43.462 --> 01:14:45.032
They're already inside.

598
01:14:45.498 --> 01:14:47.102
In the vents.

599
01:15:01.680 --> 01:15:02.852
Mason!

600
01:15:17.897 --> 01:15:19.274
Here they come!

601
01:15:26.171 --> 01:15:27.275
Viktor!

602
01:15:32.111 --> 01:15:33.351
Viktor!

603
01:15:34.113 --> 01:15:35.524
Fall back!

604
01:15:37.182 --> 01:15:39.719
No! No more running!

605
01:16:04.376 --> 01:16:06.117
Everybody in the main hall!

606
01:16:50.089 --> 01:16:52.091
- I'm out.
- We couldn't make it to the vault.

607
01:16:52.191 --> 01:16:55.191
- What the hell is going on out there?
- They're inside. They're everywhere.

608
01:16:58.097 --> 01:16:59.804
There's no time!

609
01:17:00.466 --> 01:17:02.066
No! Don't!

610
01:17:02.067 --> 01:17:03.375
No!

611
01:17:03.502 --> 01:17:06.170
Let us in! Let us in!

612
01:17:06.171 --> 01:17:08.006
- What are you doing?
- Saving our lives.

613
01:17:08.007 --> 01:17:09.173
No!

614
01:17:09.174 --> 01:17:11.120
Let us in!

615
01:17:17.182 --> 01:17:18.752
Mason!

616
01:17:42.107 --> 01:17:44.087
Doors!

617
01:17:54.987 --> 01:17:56.489
You locked us out of here...

618
01:17:57.189 --> 01:17:58.189
Yes.

619
01:17:58.190 --> 01:18:01.069
- You fucking piece of shit!
- The doors aren't gonna hold.

620
01:18:04.096 --> 01:18:05.871
We need to get the fuck outta here!

621
01:18:07.700 --> 01:18:09.236
This leads to the surface!

622
01:18:10.602 --> 01:18:13.879
You'll freeze,
if those things don't find you first.

623
01:18:29.121 --> 01:18:30.395
It's our only chance!

624
01:18:31.290 --> 01:18:32.701
No, we stay.

625
01:18:32.825 --> 01:18:34.736
- Hold them off here.
- Come on. Let's go!

626
01:18:34.860 --> 01:18:35.861
We stay!

627
01:18:36.495 --> 01:18:38.031
Just leave him.

628
01:18:39.631 --> 01:18:41.076
Come on. Come on.

629
01:18:41.600 --> 01:18:44.080
Let's go. Let's go.
Come on. Come on.

630
01:18:46.171 --> 01:18:48.378
Let's go!
Come on, all of you. Let's go!

631
01:19:04.123 --> 01:19:05.898
Nothing personal.

632
01:19:12.131 --> 01:19:13.906
You're gonna need every bullet.

633
01:19:40.492 --> 01:19:42.438
Come and get it, mother fucker.

634
01:21:06.745 --> 01:21:13.162
Oh, fuck. What do you want?

635
01:21:14.052 --> 01:21:16.658
More...

636
01:23:18.744 --> 01:23:20.746
Kai. Look.

637
01:24:08.493 --> 01:24:09.733
Sam!

638
01:24:10.429 --> 01:24:12.636
Sam! Sam!

639
01:24:22.607 --> 01:24:23.984
What do we do now?

640
01:24:31.483 --> 01:24:33.156
We walk.

641
01:24:39.224 --> 01:24:40.498
With these...

642
01:24:43.161 --> 01:24:44.902
at least we have a chance.

643
01:24:48.100 --> 01:24:49.670
Now come on.

644
01:24:50.402 --> 01:24:51.938
Come on. Let's go.

645
01:24:56.007 --> 01:24:58.817
<i>We used to live and die
by the rules we made...</i>

646
01:24:58.944 --> 01:25:00.150
Come on...

647
01:25:01.446 --> 01:25:05.451
<i>But our rules like everything
else we built...</i>

648
01:25:06.151 --> 01:25:08.062
<i>are breaking down.</i>

649
01:25:10.522 --> 01:25:12.900
<i>There's only one rule left now anyway.</i>

650
01:25:14.192 --> 01:25:15.728
<i>One rule above all...</i>

651
01:25:17.929 --> 01:25:19.237
<i>Survive.</i>

652
01:25:20.332 --> 01:25:21.777
Come on.
